---
import "../styles/global.css";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SectionNav from "../components/SectionNav.astro";
import BackLink from "../components/BackLink.astro";
import CartSheet from "../components/CartSheet.astro";
import Tracking from "../components/Tracking.astro";
import { ClientRouter } from "astro:transitions";
import TransitionHooks from "../components/TransitionHooks.astro";
import SeoHead from "../components/SeoHead.astro";
export const prerender = false;
const adminUser = Astro.locals.user;
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32.png" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16.png" />
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
  <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest" />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#1a3454" />
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
  <title>Terms of Service - Big Brain Shelf</title>
  <SeoHead title="Terms of Service - Big Brain Shelf" socialDescription="The terms that apply when you buy and read Big Brain Shelf books." />
  <meta name="description" content="The terms that apply when you buy and read Big Brain Shelf books." />
    <ClientRouter />
  <TransitionHooks />
  <Tracking />
</head>
<body class="bg-white text-stone-900 antialiased">
  <SiteHeader search cartMode="sheet" />
  <SectionNav />
  <main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-5 py-12 pb-20">
    <BackLink />
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mb-8">Last updated: October 30, 2026</p>

    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Welcome to Big Brain Shelf, a bookstore operated by Cameron Stewart in Searcy, Arkansas. By using bigbrainshelf.com or buying a book from us, you agree to these terms. Please read them through; they are written to be understood, not to hide anything. Questions are welcome at <a href="mailto:support@bigbrainshelf.com" class="text-orange-700 hover:text-orange-800">support@bigbrainshelf.com</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Who can buy</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Our books are for children, but purchases are for adults. You must be 18 or older (or the age of majority where you live) to create an account and buy from this store. Keep your account details to yourself and let us know if you think someone else has used your account.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Digital downloads and your license</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">When you buy a digital book, you are buying a license to enjoy it, not ownership of the book itself. Your license lets you download the files, keep them on your own devices, read them with your family, and print copies of the coloring pages for personal use at home or in your own classroom. The license is personal to you and cannot be transferred to anyone else.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Please do not share, redistribute, resell, or upload the files anywhere, give them away, use them commercially, or remove the copyright notices inside them. One purchase covers one household.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">So that a shared file can be traced back to its purchase, each downloaded PDF carries a small line in the bottom margin of its pages with the buying account's email address and order number, placed so it never covers the artwork, and the same purchase details are stored in the file's document information. Downloaded audiobooks carry the same purchase details in the file's tags. Each purchased file may be downloaded up to five times; if you run out, contact us and we will reset your downloads.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Printed books</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Some books are offered as full color printed books. A printed book is charged when you place your order, and we print, bind, and ship your copy after you order. Shipping is the carrier's rate for your address, rounded up to the nearest whole dollar, calculated and shown to you before you pay. You may cancel a printed book order for a full refund at any time before your copy ships, by emailing us. Printed books include the digital edition, which is yours right away.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Refunds for digital books</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">If a digital file is defective, corrupted, or we cannot deliver it, we will fix it or refund you in full. For other situations, refund requests made within 14 days of purchase are reviewed case by case; send us an email and we will do our best to make it right. Nothing in this section limits any refund rights you have under applicable law.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Intellectual property</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">The books, stories, illustrations, and the Big Brain Shelf name and logos belong to Big Brain Shelf and Cameron Stewart. Buying a book gives you the personal license described above; it does not transfer any ownership of the content itself.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Please use the store the way it is meant to be used. Do not try to access anyone else's account or downloads, interfere with the site, scrape it in a way that disrupts service, or use the books or the site for anything unlawful. We may suspend access for misuse, and we will always protect the books you have legitimately bought.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Availability and changes</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">We may add, change, or retire books and features over time, and prices may change for future purchases. Books you have already bought remain available in your library, and files you have downloaded are yours to keep under your license.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">The site and our books are provided as is. To the fullest extent allowed by law, our total liability for any claim connected to a purchase is limited to the amount you paid for the book involved, and we are not liable for indirect or consequential damages. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable law.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">We may update these terms from time to time. The current version always lives on this page with its date at the top, and continuing to use the store after an update means you accept the new version. Changes will not take away rights in books you already bought.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Governing law</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Arkansas, USA, and any disputes will be handled in the state or federal courts located in Arkansas.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">Big Brain Shelf, operated by Cameron Stewart, Searcy, Arkansas, USA. Email: <a href="mailto:support@bigbrainshelf.com" class="text-orange-700 hover:text-orange-800">support@bigbrainshelf.com</a>.</p>

    <a href="/" class="inline-block mt-10 text-sm text-stone-500 hover:text-stone-900">&larr; Back to the shelf</a>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />

  <script is:inline>
    // Keep the header account link in sync with the session. Runs now
    // and again on astro:page-load so it also applies to the header
    // swapped in by view transitions. The update is idempotent.
    function bbsAccountLink() {
      fetch("/api/auth/get-session").then(function (r) { return r.json(); }).then(function (s) {
        var link = document.getElementById("account-link");
        if (s && s.user && link) { link.textContent = "My library"; link.href = "/account"; }
      }).catch(function () {});
    }
    bbsAccountLink();
    document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", bbsAccountLink);
  </script>
<!-- cart-sheet: slide-over cart, replaces the trip to /cart for shoppers -->
<CartSheet />

</body>
</html>
